# Recipe: P2P service calls

Use `@unstoppable-stack/p2p/rpc` to define app-owned capabilities with
`defineCapability` and `procedure`. Use `/service` `serve({ storage, capability })`
on the host, issue `service.invite(['method'])`, and use
`connect({ storage, invite, contract })` on the client. Call through the returned
`api` and close both sessions at shutdown. Helpers require alpha.2 or later.

For full code read the `add-p2p-rpc` skill and the installed P2P `docs/rpc.md`.
No bare-rpc wrapper, Hyperswarm, DHT bootstrap or additional encryption layer is
needed. Reuse root `createNode` for multiple capabilities or bidirectional calls.

Validate input/output, honor stream cancellation, use explicit grants and bound
waits. Binding a contract grants nothing. Reconnect explicitly with retained
identity and peer key; mutations need app-owned idempotency. Keep native calls
in the worker and expose domain IPC to the renderer. Sessions and contracts are
not JSON objects to transfer over IPC. All P2P APIs remain experimental.
